<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <!--
  Registers the mod-storage keys this mod writes onto blocks (ADR-0012, ADR-0013).

  Why this file is required and not optional:

  MyModStorageComponent.Serialize collects RegisteredStorageGuids from every
  MyObjectBuilder_ModStorageComponentDefinition in the world and copies ONLY those keys into
  the save file. For any other key it logs

      Not saving ModStorageComponent GUID: <guid>, not claimed

  and drops the value. The data still reads back fine during the session, so the failure is
  invisible until the player reloads the world — the layout and the "Show in VGS" flags would
  simply be gone. Deleting this file therefore looks harmless and destroys player data.

  The keys must match VgsConstants.LayoutStorageKey, VgsConstants.VisibilityStorageKey,
  VgsConstants.WatchStorageKey and VgsConstants.ViewStorageKey. They are fixed forever: changing
  one loses that piece of state in every existing world.

  The first three are written on blocks; the fourth is written on the grid itself (ADR-0022) —
  the camera and the zoom describe how the construct is being looked at, so they are shared by
  every cockpit of that grid. The mechanism is the same: an entity's MyModStorageComponent is
  serialised with the entity, and only registered keys survive.

  The SubtypeId is the mod's name, so two mods claiming the same GUID produce a
  "Duplicate ModStorageComponent GUID" warning in the log instead of silently overwriting
  each other.
  -->
    <EntityComponents>
        <EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_ModStorageComponentDefinition">
            <Id>
                <TypeId>ModStorageComponent</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>VGS</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <RegisteredStorageGuids>
                <guid>0d3c1b7a-6a51-4c39-9d2e-7f8a1c4b5e60</guid>
                <guid>b1e4a2c8-77d3-4a0f-8c61-2f9e5b0d3a47</guid>
                <guid>4a7d2e19-8c63-4b0f-a51d-6e9f3c2b8d74</guid>
                <guid>7c4b9e21-5f8d-4a63-b0e7-3d19c8a6f240</guid>
            </RegisteredStorageGuids>
        </EntityComponent>
    </EntityComponents>
</Definitions>
